# Zipf 100,000 documents, 12 terms, query t0..t5, k=10, block-max MAXSCORE
#
# The regime pruning exists for. At 2,000 documents pruning still
# evaluates about 18% of the corpus, which says nothing about a real
# collection; docs/14-pruning.md said so itself.
#
# Re-baselined when MAXSCORE's probe order was fixed. Cursors are now
# probed DESCENDING by upper bound with a metadata-only block bound
# tested before every seek, so a candidate that provably cannot reach
# the threshold no longer forces the cheap cursors' seeks and decodes.
# postings_decoded fell 44% (108,452 to 60,803) and blocks_decoded 29%
# (3,831 to 2,719); blocks_skipped rose from zero because the abandoned
# candidates' seeks used to decode the blocks they now jump. Documents
# evaluated is unchanged: the same candidates survive the same bounds,
# and the equivalence property held throughout.
docs_evaluated = 501
blocks_decoded = 2719
blocks_skipped = 1108
postings_decoded = 60803
